1
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Monster Island is a animation, adventure, family
film directed by Leopoldo Aguilar.

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Young Lucas finds out he's not really a human after he surprisingly transforms
into a monster in front of the most popular kids at school.

3
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
His search for Monster Island and his real roots takes him on a fabulously scary journey that puts him face to
face with more tentacles, fangs and far-out situations than he can shake one of his new wings at.

4
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Lucas (voice), played by Phillip Adrian Vasquez.

5
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Dina / Old Lady / Teacher (voice), played by Nancy Sullivan.

6
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Carlotta / Patrick's Mom (voice), played by Katie Leigh.

7
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Veronica (voice), played by Fiona Hardingham.

8
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Kuro / Lagoon Monster (voice), played by Wally Wingert.

9
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Melanie / Cameron's Mom / Child Patrick / Monster #4 /
Monster #13 (voice), played by Jenifer Kaplan.

10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Monster Island (released as Isla Calaca in Mexico) is a 2017 English-language
Mexican animated horror comedy film directed by Leopoldo Aguilar.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
The film was produced by Ánima Estudios and animated
by India's Discreet Arts Production.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The film was first released in the United Kingdom on 21 July
2017, and later in Mexico on 14 September 2017.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
The film was released in the United States on 1
September 2017 on home media and VOD platforms.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
The film explores themes of monster, transformation, school.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
The tone is lighthearted.
